WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.401
Republican presidential candidate

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.269
and former New Jersey Governor

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.104
Chris Christie.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.638
So yesterday,

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.873
Governor, when you announced

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:07.741
that you were running for president,

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.477
you called Trump a former friend

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.678
a, quote, lonely, self

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.147
consumed, self-serving mirror hog.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.148
You've been rather

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.950
unsparing in your criticism.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.052
We should note that

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.153
you might have people out there

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.488
who are skeptical of this

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.390
because when you dropped out in 2016,

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.124
you endorsed him

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:24.991
or you ran

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.259
his transition, you helped

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.061
coach him for debates.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:28.795
What do you say to people

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:29.462
who say, you know,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.664
this guy has always been this way.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.732
You just enabled him

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.967
and now you're changing your mind?

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:34.701
Well, look,

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.069
you know, back in 20, 16,

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.303
Jake was clear to me

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.304
he was going to be the nominee.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.639
I had a long relationship with him

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.341
at that time, over 15 years,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:41.841
and I felt

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:42.542
I could help to make him

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.711
a better candidate and a better president

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.845
if he won.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.479
And I didn't

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.081
want Hillary Clinton to be president.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:50.250
And that's why I ran the first place.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.751
Turns out I was wrong.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.086
I couldn't make him a better candidate

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:53.787
and I couldn't make him

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.155
a better president.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.856
And he disappointed me.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.724
And he disappointed

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.325
a lot of people in my party.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.093
And a whole lot of people

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.027
in this country.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.395
By the way, he performed

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:02.962
and for me,

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.297
the breaking point was election night.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.365
20, 20

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.032
when he's out there

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.267
at two 30 in the morning

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.435
claiming the election was stolen

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.002
when I knew

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.438
he had no evidence to prove that.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.872
And when you want to cut democracy

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.975
in that way, you have forfeited

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.044
the trust, in my view,

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.012
to hold that office

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.847
that he's now trying to regain.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.481
And so, yeah,

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.816
I did all those things that I and

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.551
I make no apologies for them.

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.352
But when I make a misjudgment,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.120
I'll admit it.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.955
And I thought I could make him better

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.356
And then when I was up, I couldn't.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.624
In fact, he was much worse.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.827
So Trump

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.096
last night in response to you running,

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.031
ran a rather mocking

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.433
video on social media.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:40.867
There it is.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.669
It's it's you.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:43.736
I guess he's he's

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:44.737
making fun of your weight.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:46.773
That's

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.008
his we're going to be small

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.909
That's his response.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.010
What did you make of that?

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.112
What was your response to that?

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.813
You know what I saw, Jake?

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.849
I just renewed in my own mind

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.017
what a child he is.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.319
He's a baby.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.754
Whenever you want to criticize him.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.922
I mean, anyway,

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.657
that's the way he responds.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.225
And you and I

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.727
are both lucky enough to be parents

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.661
and if we had a child

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.030
who conducted themselves like that,

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.565
we'd send them to the room,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.200
not to the White House. Yeah.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.302
And I think character is destiny

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.404
for this country.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.640
And we've got to make a decision

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:21.608
about what

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.877
the character of the person should be.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.211
Who sits behind the desk

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.546
in the Oval Office.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.480
And if they're going to do that,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.248
kind of stuff.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.482
I mean, it doesn't it's.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.651
It's so childish.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.286
It's so juvenile.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:36.723
He is such a spoiled baby that,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.590
you know,

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.424
beyond that,

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.626
what he even say about

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.194
something like that, that's ridiculous.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.395
You know, I

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.998
if we want to break news here today,

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.032
I struggle with my weight

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:46.966
for about 20 years.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.668
Like tens of millions of Americans.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.937
The devil you said. Right. Exactly.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.472
So he's breaking news there.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.673
He keeps telling people something

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.941
they don't know.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.076
In the end, for me,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.846
it's about how you perform as a person.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:00.713
Yeah.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.081
What kind of heart you have.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.783
And I'll put mine up against his

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:04.517
any day in the week.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.253
So on the subject of you

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.289
admitting mistakes,

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:10.590
you were pretty candid last night

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.558
about some of those mistakes

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.992
in your speech last night.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.561
I don't have time to play the excerpt,

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:15.862
but one of the

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.396
you talked

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.564
you talked about the Bridgegate scandal.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:17.997
Right.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:19.732
And trusting people

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:20.500
you should have trusted

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.068
and also sending it.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.703
Do you admit setting a tone

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.205
that those people thought that

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.072
that would be something

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.140
that you would find acceptable?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.308
No, I didn't admit that, Jake.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.143
And I'm asking if you know, I don't.

